            display: none;
        }

        footer p {
            font-size: 0.875rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>

    <header>
        <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
    </header>

    <main id="main-content">
        <section aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
            <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <div class="example">
                <h3>
                    <button type="button" aria-controls="faq1-details">
                        Why do cats purr?
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div id="faq1-details" class="details">
                    <p>Cats purr for various reasons. While often associated with contentment, they also purr to self-soothe when stressed, injured, or even while giving birth. The frequency of a cat's purr has even been shown to aid in bone and tissue repair.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h3>
                    <button type="button" aria-controls="faq2-details">
                        Why do cats have whiskers?
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div id="faq2-details" class="details">
                    <p>Whiskers are highly sensitive tactile hairs called vibrissae. They help cats navigate in the dark, detect changes in air currents (which can indicate nearby prey), and determine if they can fit through tight spaces.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h3>
                    <button type="button" aria-controls="faq3-details">
                        Do cats always land on their feet?
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div id="faq3-details" class="details">
                    <p>Most of the time, yes, thanks to their "righting reflex." This innate ability allows them to twist their flexible spine mid-air to orient their bodies. However, this isn't foolproof; the height of the fall and the cat's health play significant roles.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="example">
                <h3>
                    <button type="button" aria-controls="faq4-details">
                        Why do cats sleep so much?
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div id="faq4-details" class="details">
                    <p>Cats are crepuscular predators, meaning they are most active at dawn and dusk. They spend an average of 12-16 hours a day sleeping to conserve energy for hunting (or playing), a trait inherited from their wild ancestors.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2024 Feline Facts Inc.</p>
    </footer>

    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
            const disclosureButtons = document.querySelectorAll('.example button[aria-controls]');

            disclosureButtons.forEach(button => {
                const panelId = button.getAttribute('aria-controls');
                const panel = document.getElementById(panelId);

                // Initialize state: collapse by default in JS
                // This ensures content is visible if JS is disabled or fails to load.
                button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
                if (panel) {
                    panel.hidden = true;
                }

                button.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    const isExpanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
                    const newExpandedState = !isExpanded;

                    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(newExpandedState));
                    if (panel) {
                        panel.hidden = isExpanded; 
                    }
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
